{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaaZdTS7YRqZBHBuLG6j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've proved `myRep_add`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem myRep_add (a : α) (m n : Nat) : myRep a (m + n) = myRep a m ++ myRep a n := by\n  induction m with\n  | zero => simp [myRep]\n  | succ m ih => rw [Nat.succ_add, myRep, myRep, ih, List.cons_append]\n```\n\nThe proof works by induction on `m`:\n- **Base case (`m = 0`):** `simp` reduces `0 + n` to `n` and `myRep a 0` to `[]`, so both sides are the same.\n- **Step case (`m + 1`):** `Nat.succ_add` rewrites `(m + 1) + n` as `(m + n) + 1`. Unfolding `myRep` on both sides gives `a :: myRep a (m + n)` on the left and `a :: myRep a m ++ myRep a n` on the right. The induction hypothesis `ih` and `List.cons_append` then make the two sides match."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":477,"cache_read_input_tokens":7871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":477},"output_tokens":352,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"933b489d-e6d1-4717-a98f-32f762b363a9","uuid":"b5abcb06-b4a2-431b-9162-c905314b5952","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:49:40.090Z","request_id":"req_011CgaaZdE3fCbP7rKARzbVy"}
